<!--
    Approval routing rules — payments and journal entries.

    Approver assignment (UIDs stable across staging/production):
      uid 9   = Fabricio Filoni  (contaduria@econovo.com.ar)
      uid 372 = Nacho Massola    (imassola@econovo.com.ar)

    Other create_uid references:
      370  = Barisone Lucas Gastón  (gbarisone@econovoagrovial.com.ar)  — COMEX
      470  = Monastra Gaspar       (gmonastra@econovo.com.ar)           — COMEX
      366  = Demarchi Agustín      (ademarchi@econovo.com.ar)           — excluded from entries
      371  = Ruiz Agustina         (contacto@econovo.com.ar)            — card expenses, excluded from entries
      482  = Varela Lourdes        (lvarela@econovo.com.ar)             — BA payments

    Company IDs (verified in production):
      1 = Econovo Agrovial S.R.L.
      2 = Oscar Scorza Equipos Y Serv. S.R.L.
      3 = Hidro Servicios de Saneamiento S.R.L. (Buenos Aires)

    EXCLUDED ACCOUNTS (Fondo Fijo + Tarjetas de crédito/débito, 46 codes):
    Sourced from finance-provided spreadsheets ("Cuentas a ignorar de
    aprobacion de pagos"), one per company. These are asset_cash accounts
    that map 1:1 to a payment journal (journal.default_account_id). Payments
    and journal entries touching any of these accounts never require
    approval, regardless of amount/company/currency, so the exclusion is
    appended to every rule's domain below.

    AMOUNT THRESHOLD RULES (noupdate="0"):
    Rules 10 and 20 use effective_approval_amount instead of amount.
    effective_approval_amount returns the batch total when the payment belongs
    to a Sumitec batch, so a 1M payment in a 5M batch is correctly routed to
    Fabricio instead of Nacho. noupdate="0" ensures the domain is re-applied
    on every module upgrade.

    ALL OTHER RULES (noupdate="1"):
    Rules 30-80 do not filter by amount and are marked noupdate="1" to protect
    any manual adjustments made through the UI after installation.
-->
<odoo>
    <!-- ============================================================
         PAGOS — rules 10 and 20: amount-threshold routing.
         noupdate="0" so domain updates (e.g. field renames) apply on upgrade.
         ============================================================ -->
    <data noupdate="0">

